<section class="os-exit">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="os-exit-k">PROTOTYPE / NOT PRODUCTION</p>
    <h2>What this page is testing.</h2>
    <p class="sub">One question: can <b>SYSTEM</b>, <b>DIAGNOSE</b> and <b>DECIDE</b> be reached as transformations of a single dealership object, rather than three separate diagrams? No node is repositioned between modes. Only the camera moves, and only emphasis changes.</p>
    <p class="sub">Modes 04–06 are stubbed deliberately. The first three carry the argument; the rest get built once this architecture is validated.</p>
    <p class="sub">The four causes — DUPLICATE, UNOWNED, INVISIBLE, WAITING — are flat peers, the same four the Diagnostic uses. BDC-01 and UC-02 share a cause and resolve to different interventions. So do SVC-06 and SVC-01. Cause constrains the intervention set; it does not determine it.</p>
  </div>
